      "post_id": 15085159,
      "ranking": null,
      "score": null,
      "tags": "[]",
      "text": "&gt; Where would you draw the line\u2026 what percentage of users would have to dislike amp for you to think it was reasonable to add an option?<p>One easy piece of math is (cost of adding and maintaining that feature) vs. [(users who dislike) x (% of users who would quit you) x (profit per user)]<p>For example, if 10% of all users disliked it (300M users), but only 1% of those would leave your services (3M users) and you made, on average, $10 per user in profit, you&#x27;d be putting $30M&#x2F;year of profit at risk, which is probably enough to hire a few people to build and maintain that feature.",
      "time": 1503588429,
      "timestamp": 1503588429000000,
      "title": "",
      "type": "comment",
      "url": ""
    },
